  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\n1. **Identify upgrade options** for the cheapest base model of the MacBook Pro 14-inch with M5 chip\n2. **Calculate the total price difference** from the base model to the maximum upgrade (no Pre-Installed Software)\n\n## Verification Against Screenshots\n\n**Screenshot 5 (Model selection):** Shows \"Shop MacBook Pro\" page with the 14-inch model selected (\"Buy from $1999\") and the 16-inch option (\"Buy from $2999\"). Critically, the header shows **\"Buy for $4,069.00\"** — confirming the maximum upgraded configuration total price.\n\n**Screenshot 2 (Chip selection):** Confirms the M5 chip is selected as the cheapest option (\"Buy from $1999 or $166.58/mo.\"), with 10-core CPU, 10-core GPU, 16-core Neural Engine. M5 Pro ($2499) and M5 Max ($4099) are more expensive, confirming M5 is the cheapest base chip.\n\n**Screenshot 1 (Color/Display):** Confirms the base configuration starting at $1999 with Space Black color and Standard display selected.\n\n## Verification of Response Content\n\nThe response lists:\n- **Base model:** 14-inch MacBook Pro M5 (16GB/1TB, 70W adapter, standard display) = $1999 ✓ (confirmed in screenshots)\n- **Upgrade options:** Nano-texture display (+$150), Memory 24GB (+$200)/32GB (+$400), Storage 2TB (+$500)/4TB (+$1,500), 96W adapter (+$20), Keyboard localization (no charge), Pre-Installed Software excluded\n- **Maximum upgrade price:** $4069 ✓ (confirmed in Screenshot 5: \"Buy for $4,069.00\")\n\n**Mathematical verification:**\n- Maximum config: $1999 + $150 + $400 + $1,500 + $20 = **$4069** ✓ (matches screenshot)\n- Price difference: $4069 − $1999 = **$2070** ✓ (also equals $150 + $400 + $1,500 + $20 = $2070)\n\nThe individual upgrade option prices are not legible in the compressed screenshots, but per evaluation guidelines, content in the response not visible in screenshots can be believed. The key verifiable figures ($1999 base and $4069 maximum) are both confirmed in the screenshots, and the calculation is internally consistent.\n\nBoth parts of the task (identifying upgrade options and calculating the price difference) were completed correctly.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**SUCCESS**",
